    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d96">

                <pb facs="0208" n="104" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg104"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wharton to Mr. Mizner</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-09-15"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 15,
                        1890</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 174.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your No. 147 of
                    the 27th ultimo, in which you repeat the instructions sent you relative to the
                    employment of the, concurrent good offices of the United States and Mexico to
                    bring about peace in Central America.</p>
                <p>The desired peace having already been secured prior to the occurrence of an
                    opportunity to act on those instructions, the telegram of the 19th ultimo, which
                    you quote, is no longer of special pertinence.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William F. Wharton</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
